the true death toll from Kovac 19 is  revealed in the latest official figures  from the office for national statistics  they've looked at the average number of  people who would be expected to die for  the time of year in England and Wales  and they added in the death  registrations for 2020 in all there have  been more than 46,000 extra death  between the start of the epidemic in  March and the beginning of May these  excess deaths as they're called include  not just those with Kovach 19 recorded  on their death certificate but also  deaths attributed to other causes and  the stats show there were 13,000 extra  non-coated 19 deaths over this period of  these the biggest increase over the  long-term average was in deaths  attributed to dementia up 52 percent  it's likely that these were care home  residents whose lives were cut short by  the virus even if that wasn't reflected  on their death certificate and has also  been a big increase in death from causes  such as asthma and diabetes in mid April  they spiked at 197 percent and 161  percent above average and they were  outside hospital so it's likely to  reflect a reluctance to seek medical  attention during the epidemic but a  second report by the ons shows the  epidemic is tailing off 53,000 people in  England had the virus in their latest  household survey that's hard down from  133,000 last week in fact the ONS says  there is a steady fall now more than  0.4% of the population were infected at  the end of April by the end of May it  was just 0.1% although there are still  five and a half thousand people a day  catching the virus the latest estimate  of the our number is 0.7 to 0.9 below  the key threshold of 1 indicating that  the spread of the virus is slowing but  these stats predate the easing of the  lockdown  earlier this week we'll see in the  coming days whether more social contact  has increased spread of the virus
 

